/ A line of HTML is handed to the HTML grammar, which can be left open across lines the way a
/ filter's grammar can - a tag, a comment, a <script>. The sentinel word stands for one of those.
/ An HTML line is one line of Slim, so the line below it must be a Slim line again.
<p LEFT_OPEN_BY_THE_STUB
p after an open tag
div
  <span LEFT_OPEN_BY_THE_STUB
  p sibling of the html
p after a nested html line
p inline <b LEFT_OPEN_BY_THE_STUB
p after inline html
/ Upstream also ended this rule at a `/>`, which handed the rest of the line back to Slim and read
/ `= b` as Ruby. Slim renders it as the text it is, so the whole line is HTML.
<div>a/> = b
